936878X"],"issn_org":["1936878X"],"issue":"7","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"834-837","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008582316"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ceb23d4d-858d-44f0-9323-b17296b8e744"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Good FFRCT Test-Retest Reproducibility : The Importance of High Coronary CT Angiography Image Quality","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816676","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: With the increasing use of coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), the prevalence of patients with non-obstructive atherosclerotic coronary artery disease (NOCAD) is growing. Presence of NOCAD is associated with an increased risk of an unfavorable clinical outcome. Therefore, guideline-directed preventive strategies such as lipid-lowering therapy with statins are important. This study aims to assess whether visualization of personal CTA images to patients with a new diagnosis of NOCAD facilitates reduction of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol (primary endpoint), improves statin adherence, influences the perception of statin-associated side effects, and modifies the coronary atherosclerotic phenotype. METHODS: The VICAD-RISK study is a Danish multicenter randomized trial including statin naïve patients suspected of chronic coronary syndrome with a new diagnosis of NOCAD determined by first-line coronary CTA. A total of 273 patients will be randomized 1:1:1 into; (1) usual care; representing current clinical practice of general practitioner follow-up; (2) low-intensity intervention; specialized nurse consultation, or (3) high-intensity intervention; similar to group 2 and presentation of the personal CTA-images. All participants, including the intervention groups, will be followed at the discretion of their general practitioner. Research follow-up including biochemistry measurements, and coronary CTA investigation will be repeated for all participants after 12 months. CONCLUSION: The VICAD-RISK study evaluates whether personal CTA image visualization in patients with a new diagnosis of NOCAD improves reduction of LDL cholesterol. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT06413641, www. CLINICALTRIALS: gov.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Kulasingam, Archana","Laustsen, Sussie","Busk, Martin","Sand, Niels-Peter Rønnow","Winther, Simon","Kragholm, Kristian","Hammid, Osama","Pedersen, Kamilla Bech","Vedsted, Peter","Kanstrup, Helle","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S03-099.89-822236"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Kulasingam, Archana"],"keyword":["Cholesterol LDL blood","Computed Tomography Angiography methods","Coronary Angiography methods","Coronary Artery Disease diagnostic imaging","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl CoA Reductase Inhibitors therapeutic use","Male","Middle Aged","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Danish Private Medical Clinic (Danske Speciallæger)"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rationale and design of vicad risk study visualization of coronary artery disease for modification of risk factors","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ahj.2025.04.002","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We acknowledge the Novo Nordisk Foundation and the Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University, for financial support. Moreover, we thank the study nurses and the radiologic technologists from each participating site, as well as the study patients participating in this study. This study was funded by an unrestricted research grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF21OC0068200 ). The study is investigator-initiated, and the authors are solely responsible for the study design, data collection, analyses and writing of manuscripts."],"id":"S03-099.89-822236","identifier":[{"id":"105003422280","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40187715","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-0fada2d3-e58b-4f85-b63b-473f0768b155","au-1ccf07d8-b648-4760-b4c6-c464a5144bbe","sdu-9ad46e02-c4fc-4858-803c-a184bad45fb8"],"keyword":["Cholesterol, LDL/blood","Computed Tomography Angiography/methods","Coronary Angiography/methods","Coronary Artery Disease/diagnostic imaging","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA Reductase Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Male","Middle Aged","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-1C0D4EC8C644FFE31462682524931A2B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289301372/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/792739124/Rationale_and_design_of_VICAD-RISK_study_Visualization_of_coronary_artery_disease_for_modification_of_risk_factors_2025_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ahj.2025.04.002","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"n