-465a-bf82-9b47f5351bb2","au-882a0510-9caf-425d-b74f-01664b4f6f10","sdu-65f2b6a4-8f9e-49ff-8ed2-768e9d0ed95d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of Autoimmune Diseases With Coronary Atherosclerosis Severity and Ischemic Events","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-741264","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The association between coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA) derived fractional flow reserve (FFRCT) and risk of recurrent angina in patients with new onset stable angina pectoris (SAP) and stenosis by CTA is uncertain. METHODS: Multicenter 3-year follow-up study of patients presenting with symptoms suggestive of new onset SAP who underwent first-line CTA evaluation and subsequent standard-of-care treatment. All patients had at least one ≥30 ​% coronary stenosis. A per-patient lowest FFRCT-value ≤0.80 represented an abnormal test result. Patients with FFRCT ≤0.80 who underwent revascularization were categorized according to completeness of revascularization: 1) Completely revascularized (CR-FFRCT), all vessels with FFRCT ≤0.80 revascularized; or 2) incompletely revascularized (IR-FFRCT) ≥1 vessels with FFRCT ≤0.80 non-revascularized. Recurrent angina was evaluated using the Seattle Angina Questionnaire. RESULTS: Amongst 769 patients (619 [80 ​%] stenosis ≥50 ​%, 510 [66 ​%] FFRCT ≤0.80), 174 (23 ​%) reported recurrent angina at follow-up. An FFRCT ≤0.80 vs ​> ​0.80 associated to increased risk of recurrent angina, relative risk (RR): 1.82; 95 ​% CI: 1.31-2.52, p ​< ​0.001. Risk of recurrent angina in CR-FFRCT (n ​= ​135) was similar to patients with FFRCT >0.80, 13 ​% vs 15 ​%, RR: 0.93; 95 ​% CI: 0.62-1.40, p ​= ​0.72, while IR-FFRCT (n ​= ​90) and non-revascularized patients with FFRCT ≤0.80 (n ​= ​285) had increased risk, 37 ​% vs 15 ​% RR: 2.50; 95 ​% CI: 1.68-3.73, p ​< ​0.001 and 30 ​% vs 15 ​%, RR: 2.03; 95 ​% CI: 1.44-2.87, p ​< ​0.001, respectively. Use of antianginal medication was similar across study groups. CONCLUSION: In patients with SAP and coronary stenosis by CTA undergoing standard-of-care guided treatment, FFRCT provides information regarding risk of recurrent angina.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Madsen, Kristian Tækker","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Øvrehus, Kristian Altern","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Parner, Erik Thorlund","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Fairbairn, Timothy A","Nieman, Koen","Patel, Manesh R","Rogers, Campbell","Mullen, Sarah","Mickley, Hans","Thomsen, Kristian Korsgaard","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Leipsic, Jonathon","Sand, Niels Peter Rønnow"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735201"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Kristian Tækker"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Duke University Medical Center","Heartflow Inc.","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Royal Liverpool and Broadgreen University Hospitals NHS Trust","Stanford University","University of British Columbia","University of British Columbia (UBC)"],"keyword":["Aged","Angina","Angina Stable physiopathology","Complete revascularization","Computed Tomography Angiography","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Stenosis diagnostic imaging","Coronary Vessels diagnostic imaging","Coronary computed tomography angiography","Coronary revascularization","FFR","Female","Follow Up Studies","Fractional Flow Reserve Myocardial","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Recurrence","Recurrent angina","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Severity of Illness Index","Stable angina pectoris","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coronary computed tomography angiography derived fractional flow reserve and risk of recurrent angina a 000000000003 year follow up study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-gr