avid J","key":"brooksdavidjpau","last":"Brooks","locid":"3ea60c0d-a602-4a6f-a037-7477fddb7c50","name":"Brooks, David J","orcid":"0000-0003-2602-2518","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"vorupjensenthomaspau","last":"Vorup-Jensen","locid":"77b03498-95a4-453b-81a8-e2c05fa0ca0c","name":"Vorup-Jensen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-4140-6563","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38336934"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-45627-y","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"1224","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184720923"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b5519e3f-a90c-446b-a3c6-e34875c060aa","sdu-af61a252-984a-4041-83e3-c53bd9942836"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Amyloid-β aggregates activate peripheral monocytes in mild cognitive impairment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-724810","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: The prognostic impact of complete coronary revascularization relative to non-invasive testing methods is unknown. Objectives: To assess the association between completeness of revascularization defined by CTA-derived fractional flow reserve (FFRCT) and cardiovascular outcomes in patients with stable angina. Methods: Multicenter 3-year follow-up study of patients with new onset stable angina and ≥ 30% stenosis by CTA. The lesion-specific FFRCT value (two cm-distal-to-stenosis) was registered in all vessels with stenosis and considered abnormal when ≤ 0.80. Patients with FFRCT ≤ 0.80 were categorized as: Completely revascularized (CR-FFRCT), all vessels with FFRCT ≤ 0.80 revascularized; incompletely revascularized (IR-FFRCT), ≥ 1 vessels with FFRCT ≤ 0.80 non-revascularized. Early revascularization (< 90 days from index CTA) categorized vessels as revascularized. The primary endpoint comprised cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction; the secondary endpoint vessel-specific late revascularization and non-fatal myocardial infarction. Results: Amongst 900 patients and 1759 vessels, FFRCT was ≤ 0.80 in 377 (42%) patients, 536 (30%) vessels; revascularization was performed in 244 (27%) patients, 340 (19%) vessels. Risk of the primary endpoint was higher for IR-FFRCT (15/210 [7.1%]) compared to CR-FFRCT (4/167 [2.4%]), RR: 2.98; 95% CI: 1.01–8.8, p ​= ​0.036, and to normal FFRCT (3/523 [0.6%]), RR: 12.45; 95% CI: 3.6–42.6, p ​< ​0.001. Incidence of the secondary endpoint was higher in non-revascularized vessels with FFRCT ≤ 0.80 (29/250 [12%]) compared to revascularized vessels with FFRCT ≤ 0.80 (5/286 [1.7%]), p ​= ​0.001, and to vessels with FFRCT > 0.80 (10/1223 [0.8%]), p ​< ​0.001. Conclusion: Incomplete revascularization of patients with lesion-specific FFRCT ≤ 0.80 is associated to unfavorable cardiovascular outcomes compared to those with complete revascularization or FFRCT > 0.80.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Madsen, Kristian Tækker","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Øvrehus, Kristian Altern","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Parner, Erik Thorlund","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Iraqi, Nadia","Fairbairn, Timothy A","Nieman, Koen","Patel, Manesh R","Rogers, Campbell","Mullen, Sarah","Mickley, Hans","Thomsen, Kristian Korsgaard","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Leipsic, Jonathon","Rønnow Sand, Niels Peter"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767945"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Kristian Tækker"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Duke University Medical Center","Heartflow Inc.","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Stanford University","University of British Columbia","University of British Columbia (UBC)"],"keyword":["Aged","Angina Stable physiopathology","Computed Tomography Angiography","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease diagnostic imaging","Coronary Stenosis diagnostic imaging","Coronary Vessels diagnostic imaging","Coronary artery disease","Coronary computed tomography angiography","Coronary revascularization","FFR","Female","Fractional Flow Reserve Myocardial","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Myocardial Infarction mortality","Myocardial Revascularization","Predictive Value of Tests","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Severity of Illness Index","Stable angina pectoris","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"completeness of revascularization