k","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathon","key":"leipsicpau","last":"Leipsic","name":"Leipsic, Jonathon","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Peter R.","key":"sandpau","last":"Sand","locid":"167f1566-1eb7-495f-be19-63a30a43aff1","name":"Sand, Niels Peter","name_org":"Sand, Niels Peter R.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37698477"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1148/radiol.230524","issn":["00338419","15271315"],"issn_org":["00338419"],"issue":"3","journal":"Radiology","paperid":"e230524","publisher":"Radiological Society of North America Inc.","status":"p","title":"Radiology","volume":"308"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170627772"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-27145536-d4f2-40c7-b3cd-8dae4ad358ff","sdu-2668b17f-8bcb-4552-b62f-fd8780592abd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prognostic Value of Coronary CT Angiography-derived Fractional Flow Reserve on 3-year Outcomes in Patients with Stable Angina","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-691931","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: During treatment with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) such as the anti-PD-1 antibody pembrolizumab, half of patients with pre-existing inflammatory arthritis experience disease flares. The underlying immunological mechanisms have not been characterized. Here, we investigate the effect of pembrolizumab on cells involved in inflammation and destruction in the synovial joint and how immunosuppressive treatments affect the pembrolizumab-induced immune reactions. Methods: We included synovial fluid mononuclear cells (SFMCs, n = 28) and peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs, n = 6) from patients with rheumatoid arthritis and peripheral spondyloarthritis and PBMCs from healthy controls (n = 6). Fibroblast-like synovial cells (FLSs) were grown from SFMCs. The in vitro effect of pembrolizumab was tested in SFMCs cultured for 48 h, FLS-PBMC co-cultures and in SFMCs cultured for 21 days (inflammatory osteoclastogenesis). Cells and supernatants were analyzed by ELISA, flow cytometry, and pro-inflammatory multiplex assay. Finally, the effect of the disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (DMARDs) adalimumab (TNFα inhibitor), tocilizumab (IL-6R inhibitor), tofacitinib (JAK1/JAK3 inhibitor), and baricitinib (JAK1/JAK2 inhibitor) on pembrolizumab-induced immune reactions was tested. Results: Pembrolizumab significantly increased monocyte chemoattractant protein-1 (MCP-1) production by arthritis SFMCs (P = 0.0031) but not by PBMCs from patients or healthy controls (P = 0.77 and P = 0.43). Pembrolizumab did not alter MMP-3 production in FLS-PBMC co-cultures (P = 0.76) or TRAP secretion in the inflammatory osteoclastogenesis model (P = 0.28). In SFMCs, pembrolizumab further increased the production of TNFα (P = 0.0110), IFNγ (P = 0.0125), IL-12p70 (P = 0.0014), IL-10 (P = 0.0100), IL-13 (P = 0.0044), IL-2 (P = 0.0066), and IL-4 (P = 0.0008) but did not change the production of IL-6 (P = 0.1938) and IL-1 (P = 0.1022). The SFMCs treated with pembrolizumab showed an increased frequency of intermediate monocytes (P = 0.044), and the MCP-1 production increased only within the intermediate monocyte subset (P = 0.028). Lastly, adalimumab, baricitinib, and tofacitinib treatment were able to attenuate the pembrolizumab-induced MCP-1 production (P = 0.0004, P = 0.033, and P = 0.025, respectively), while this was not seen with tocilizumab treatment (P = 0.75). Conclusion: Pembrolizumab specifically activated intermediate monocytes and induced the production of several cytokines including TNFα but not IL-6. These findings indicate that flares in patients with pre-existing inflammatory arthritis involve monocyte activation and could be managed with TNFα neutralization.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anne Sofie","Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","Juul-Madsen, Kristian","Broksø, Amalie Dyrelund","Skejø, Cæcilie","Schmidt, Henrik","Vorup-Jensen, Thomas","Kragstrup, Tue Wenzel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-198407"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kragstrup, Tue Wenzel"],"keyword":["Antibody","Arthritis","Arthritis Rheumatoid","Autoimmunity","Binding","Bone destruction","Cancer","Cells Cultured","Classification criteria","Cytokine","Humans","Immune checkpoint inhibitors","Immunology","Immunotherapy","Leukocytes Mononuclear","Monocyte","Monocytes","PD 1","Receptor","Rheumatoid arthritis","Safety","Spondyloarthritis","Synovial fluid","TARGET","Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha pharmacology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tumor necrosis factor alpha neutralization attenuates immune checkpoint inhibitor induced activation of intermediate monocytes in synovial fluid mononuclear cells from patients with inflammatory arthritis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13075-022-02737-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-198407","identifier":[{"id":"000755130000002","type":"wos"},{"id":"85124975721","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35164829","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8842914","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-78c6adcf-fb9d-401e-839b-a89ccd2410bc"],"keyword":["ANTIBODY","Arthritis","Arthritis, Rheumatoid","BINDING","BONE DESTRUCTION","CLASSIFICATION CRITERIA","Cells, Cultured","Cytokine","Humans","Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors","Immunology","Immunotherapy","Leukocytes, Mononuclear","Monocyte","Monocytes","PD-1","RECEPTOR","RHEUMATOID-ARTHRITIS","SAFETY","SPONDYLOARTHRITIS","Synovial Fluid","TARGET","Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha/pharmacology","autoimmunity","cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FFAE25940E5CC7604864B5A844E959A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13075-022-02737-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Sofie","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"af561ec5-e4d0-48ec-9462-3e7b00c11efc","name":"Sørensen, Anne Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Nørgaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5820fa2e-0f0e-4429-badc-9e264f102231","name":"Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0820-7789","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"juulmadsenpau","last":"Juul-Madsen","locid":"e1f1360b-467e-4b44-b1c1-d5c6a0da4acf","name":"Juul-Madsen, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-5309-5221","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalie Dyrelund","key":"broksøpau","last":"Broksø","locid":"4d7e7463-1a8d-47bc-bcc2-cd3ddfb93a25","name":"Broksø, Amalie Dyrelund","orcid":"0009-0008-1144-9440","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie","key":"skejøpau","last":"Skejø","locid":"51d88bd5-50cb-4c5f-aa4c-242af4b40932","name":"Skejø, Cæcilie","orcid":"0000-0002-7965-399X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"834188a5-a600-41a5-a8a1-9e34c3837141","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"vorupjensenpau","last":"Vorup-Jensen","locid":"77b03498-95a4-453b-81a8-e2c05fa0ca0c","name":"Vorup-Jensen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-4140-6563","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tue Wenzel","key":"kragstruppau","last":"Kragstrup","locid":"e1e2fde6-99ce-4d01-b3d4-5c8160d80136","name":"Kragstrup, Tue Wenzel","orcid":"0000-0002-6439-397X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35164829"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13075-022-02737-6","issn":["14786354","14786362"],"issn_org":["14786354"],"issue":"1","journal":"Arthritis Research and Therapy","paperid":"43","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Arthritis Research and Therapy","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124975721"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-78c6adcf-fb9d-401e-839b-a89ccd2410bc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tumor necrosis factor alpha neutralization attenuates immune checkpoint inhibitor-induced activation of intermediate monocytes in synovial fluid mononuclear cells from patients with inflammatory arthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-198407","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aggregated data obtained from job postings provide powerful insights into labor market demands, and emerging skills, and aid job matching. However, most extraction approaches are supervised and thus need costly and time-consuming annotation. To overcome this, we propose Skill Extraction with Weak Supervision. We leverage the European Skills, Competences, Qualifications and Occupations taxonomy to find similar skills in job ads via latent representations. The method shows a strong positive signal, outperforming baselines based on token-level and syntactic patterns.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382326"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Emerging skills","Labor market demands","Latent representations","Skill Extraction","Weak supervision"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skill extraction from job postings using weak supervision","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2209.08071","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382326","ids":["itu-4735afc6-4ec5-480d-a806-0c23dd07bd04"],"keyword":["Emerging skills","Labor market demands","Latent representations","Skill extraction","Weak supervision"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D3B0CACAE657F553EED864560E039C23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87084650/RecSysHR2022_paper_10.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2209.08071","version":"Published Version"},{"access":