ull,"first":"Connie","key":"zieglerpau","last":"Ziegler","name":"Ziegler, Connie","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2 10","corresponding":null,"first":"Merete Lund","key":"hetlandpau","last":"Hetland","name":"Hetland, Merete Lund","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/annrheumdis-2022-eular.2234","issn":["00034967","14682060"],"issn_org":["00034967"],"issue":"suppl. 1","journal":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","pages":"944-945","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen center for arthritis research (copecare)","the danbio registry","zitelab aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-80a180b2-1705-4502-8bc3-743b02b30c0b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Clinical factors associated with a positive SARS-CoV-19 test and with frequent testing during the COVID-19 pandemic in &gt;10.000 patients with inflammatory rheumatic diseases. Results from a nationwide survey from the Danish DANBIO registry","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-610016","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Diabetes mellitus is a major risk factor for coronary artery disease (CAD) and may provoke structural and functional changes in coronary vasculature. The coronary volume to left ventricular mass (V/M) ratio is a new anatomical parameter capable of revealing a potential physiological imbalance between coronary vasculature and myocardial mass. The aim of this study was to examine the V/M derived from coronary computed tomography angiography (CCTA) in patients with diabetes. METHODS: Patients with clinically suspected CAD enrolled in the ADVANCE (Assessing Diagnostic Value of Non-invasive FFRCT in Coronary Care) registry and known diabetic status were included. Coronary artery volume and left ventricular myocardial mass were analyzed from CCTA and the V/M ratio was calculated and compared between patients with and without diabetes. RESULTS: Of the 3053 patients (age 66 ​± ​10 years; 66% male) with known diabetic status, diabetes was present in 21.9%. Coronary volume was lower in patients with diabetes compared to those without diabetes (2850 ​± ​940 ​mm3 vs. 3040 ​± ​970 ​mm3, p ​< ​0.0001), whereas the myocardial mass was comparable between the 2 groups (122 ​± ​33 ​g vs. 122 ​± ​32 ​g, p ​= ​0.70). The V/M ratio was significantly lower in patients with diabetes (23.9 ​± ​6.8 ​mm3/g vs. 25.7 ​± ​7.5 ​mm3/g, p ​< ​0.0001). Among subjects with obstructive CAD (n ​= ​2191, 24.0% diabetics) and non-obstructive CAD (16.7% diabetics), the V/M ratio was significantly lower in patients with diabetes compared to those without (23.4 ​± ​6.7 ​mm3/g vs. 25.0 ​± ​7.3 ​mm3/g, p ​< ​0.0001 and 25.6 ​± ​6.9 ​mm3/g vs. 27.3 ​± ​7.6 ​mm3/g, respectively, p ​= ​0.006). CONCLUSION: The V/M ratio was significantly lower in patients with diabetes compared to non-diabetics, even after correcting for obstructive coronary stenosis. The clinical value of the reduced V/M ratio in diabetic patients needs further investigation.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Kuneman, Jurrien H","El Mahdiui, Mohammed","van Rosendael, Alexander R","van den Hoogen, Inge J","Patel, Manesh R","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Fairbairn, Timothy A","Nieman, Koen","Akasaka, Takashi","Berman, Daniel S","Hurwitz Koweek, Lynne M","Pontone, Gianluca","Kawasaki, Tomohiro","Rønnow Sand, Niels Peter","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Amano, Tetsuya","Poon, Michael","Øvrehus, Kristian A","Sonck, Jeroen","Rabbat, Mark G","De Bruyne, Bernard","Rogers, Campbell","Matsuo, Hitoshi","Bax, Jeroen J","Leipsic, Jonathon A","Knuuti, Juhani"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-028273"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Knuuti, Juhani"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Finland","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aichi Medical University","All Global Affiliations","Cardiovascular Center of Aalst","Cedars-Sinai Comprehensive Cancer Center","Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","Duke Clinical Research Institute","Duke University","Gifu Heart Center","Heartflow Inc.","IRCCS Centro Cardiologico Monzino","IRCCS Centro Cardiologico S.P.A. Fondazione Monzino - Milano","Leiden University","Liverpool John Moores University","Loyola University","Loyola University Chicago","Northwell Health","OLV Hospital Aalst","Shin Koga Hospital","Shin Koga Hospital, Fukuoka, Japan.","St. Pauls Hospital","Stanford University","University of Liverpool","University of Naples Federico II","University of Turku","Wakayama Medical University"],"keyword":["Aged","Computed Tomography Angiography","Coronary Angiography methods","Coronary Artery Disease diagnostic imaging","Coronary Stenosis","Coronary artery disease","Coronary computed tomography angiography","Coronary volume","Diabetes Mellitus diagnosis","Diabetes mellitus","Female","Humans","Left ventricular mass","Male","Middle Aged","Predictive Value o