{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The ADVANCE registry is a large prospective study of outcomes and resource utilization in patients undergoing coronary computed tomography angiography (CCTA) and CT-based fractional flow reserve (FFRCT). As experience with new technologies and practices develops over time, we investigated temporal changes in the use of FFRCT within the ADVANCE registry. METHODS: 5083 patients with coronary artery disease (CAD) on CCTA were prospectively enrolled in the ADVANCE registry and were divided into 3 equally sized cohorts based on the temporal order of enrollment per site. Demographics, CCTA and FFRCT findings, and clinical outcomes through 1-year follow-up, were recorded and compared between tertiles. RESULTS: The number of patients with a ≥70% stenosis on CCTA was similar over time (33.6%, 30.9%, and 33.8% for cohort 1-3). The rate of positive FFRCT ≤0.80 was higher for cohorts 2 (67.3%) and 3 (74.6%) than for cohort 1 (57.1%, p < 0.001). Invasive FFR rates decreased from 25.8% to 22.4% between cohort 1 and 3 (p = 0.023). Moreover, patients with a FFRCT ≤0.80 were less frequently referred for invasive coronary angiography (ICA) (from 62.9% to 52.9%, p < 0.001), and underwent fewer revascularizations between cohort 1 and 3 (from 41.9% to 32.0%, p < 0.001). The prevalence of major events was low (1.2%) and similar between cohorts. CONCLUSIONS: Growing experience with FFRCT improved the likelihood of identifying hemodynamically significant CAD and safely reduced the need for ICA and revascularization in patients with anatomically significant disease even in the instance of an abnormal FFRCT.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Nous, Fay","Budde, Ricardo P J","Fairbairn, Timothy A","Akasaka, Takashi","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Berman, Daniel S","Raff, Gilbert","Hurwitz-Koweek, Lynne M","Pontone, Gianluca","Kawasaki, Tomohiro","Sand, Niels Peter R","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Amano, Tetsuya","Poon, Michael","Øvrehus, Kristian A","Sonck, Jeroen","Rabbat, Mark G","Mullen, Sarah","De Bruyne, Bernard","Rogers, Campbell","Matsuo, Hitoshi","Bax, Jeroen J","Leipsic, Jonathon","Patel, Manesh R","Nieman, Koen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-020993"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nieman, Koen"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Germany","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aichi Medical University","All Global Affiliations","Beaumont Academic Heart and Vascular Group","CardioVascular Center Frankfurt CVC","Cardiovascular Center of Aalst","Cedars-Sinai Comprehensive Cancer Center","Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","Duke Clinical Research Institute","Duke University","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Gifu Heart Center","Heartflow Inc.","IRCCS Centro Cardiologico Monzino","Leiden University","Liverpool John Moores University","Loyola University","Loyola University Chicago","Northwell Health","OLV Hospital Aalst","Shin Koga Hospital","Stanford University","University of British Columbia (UBC)","University of California at Berkeley","University of Liverpool","University of Naples Federico II","Wakayama Medical University"],"keyword":["Angina","Computerized tomography","Coronary artery disease","Fractional flow reserve","Ischemia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal changes in ffr sub ct sub guided management of coronary artery disease lessons from the advance registry","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85085133776","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Dr. Nous has received travel sponsorship from HeartFlow. Dr. Fairbairn has served on the Speakers Bureau for HeartFlow. Dr. Nørgaard has received unrestricted institutional research grants from Siemens and HeartFlow. Dr. Berman has received unrestricted research support from HeartFlow. Dr. Hurwitz-Koweek has received research support and fee as speaker from HeartFlow and Siemens . Dr. Pontone has received research grant and/or fee as speaker from GE Healthcare , Bracco, and HeartFlow. Dr. Budde has institutional research support from HeartFlow and Siemens Healthineers . Dr. Sonck has received research grant support from the Cardiopath PhD program. Dr. Rabbat has served as a consultant for HeartFlow. Dr. Mullen is an employee of and owns equity in HeartFlow. Dr. De Bruyne has received consulting fees from Abbott , Opsens, and Boston Scientific; and is a shareholder for Siemens , GE Healthcare , Bayer , Philips , HeartFlow, Edwards Lifesciences , and Sanofi . Dr. Rogers is employee of and owns equity in HeartFlow. Dr. Leipsic has served as a consultant for and owns stock options in Circle CVI and HeartFlow. Dr. Patel has received research grants from HeartFlow, Bayer , Janssen, and the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute; and has served on the advisory board for HeartFlow, Bayer , and Janssen. Dr. Nieman has received institutional research support from Siemens Healthineers , HeartFlow, GE Healthcare , and Bayer Healthcare. All other authors have reported that they have no relationships relevant to the contents of this paper to disclose."],"id":"S02-100.00-020993","identifier":[{"id":"85085133776","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32418861","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-71c23703-cf9c-4f1c-9ca9-12fda06d799d","sdu-c6340063-f731-4e37-843c-436bf0805f6d"],"keyword":["Angina","Computerized tomography","Coronary artery disease","Fractional flow res