 Drage","orcid":"0000-0001-6124-8972","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"møllersørensenchristianpau","last":"Møller Sørensen","locid":"3258a089-7c27-4849-8366-5a58c8a5fa26","name":"Møller Sørensen, Christian","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Møller","key":"sørensenchristianmøllerpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Christian Møller","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Steen","key":"kroghnielssteenpau","last":"Krogh","name":"Krogh, Niels Steen","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"nørgaardagerbojettepau","last":"Nørgaard Agerbo","name":"Nørgaard Agerbo, Jette","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette Nørgaard","key":"agerbojettenørgaardpau","last":"Agerbo","name":"Agerbo, Jette Nørgaard","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Connie","key":"zieglerconniepau","last":"Ziegler","name":"Ziegler, Connie","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete Lund","key":"hetlandmeretelundpau","last":"Hetland","locid":"3407b4a7-174d-43db-bae6-74e7f035a81f","name":"Hetland, Merete Lund","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34146099"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/rheumatology/keab500","issn":["14620324","14620332"],"issn_org":["14620324"],"issue":"SI","journal":"Rheumatology","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Rheumatology","title_org":"Rheumatology (Oxford, England)","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118285880"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","zitelab","zitelab aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bd39b087-5ede-4e0d-92f3-c532bbdbd917","ku-756ad29f-55b4-4aba-88fd-1f15507cdf2b","sdu-911c6d61-3d12-4a89-b8c2-55d4ce57e991"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on treat-to-target strategies and physical consultations in &gt;7000 patients with inflammatory arthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-085.22-026416","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Understanding the influence of physical drivers and their scale-dependent interactions on ecosystem structure and function is becoming increasingly relevant as ecologists are challenged to quantify and predict the biological implications of anthropogenic activities and climate changes. Here, we aim to quantify the impact of multiple physical drivers (ice scour, wave exposure, and air temperature) and their interactions with small scale modifying factors (tidal level, substrate rugosity, and canopy forming macroalgae) on rocky intertidal community structure. We did this by quantifying intertidal biomass, cover and species richness at three tidal levels (high, mid, and low) at four sites in a sub-arctic Greenland fjord. We found a well-developed intertidal community, with a total of 16 macroalgae and 20 invertebrate species. At one locality, the total biomass was dominated by canopy forming algae exceeding 16 kg wet weight per m –2. Physical stress from ice scour, waves, and air exposure had negative effects on all three community metrics but important interactions and modifying processes were identified. The effect of tidal level differed between sites ranging from an absence of organisms at both high- and mid-intertidal level at the most ice- and wave exposed site to extensive cover across all three tidal levels at the wave and ice sheltered site. Canopy forming macroalgae and substrate rugosity both modified the impacts of physical stress. In the absence of ice scour, canopy forming algae formed extensive cover that modified extreme air temperatures, and the abundance of dominant invertebrate species were all positively related to the biomass of macroalgae. Rugosity provided refuge from ice scour, facilitating increased species richness and cover at exposed sites. Moreover, we detected no negative effects of fast ice, and ice scour impacts were primarily found where presence of glacial ice was combined with wave exposure. Our results provide an example of how large-scale physical factors pass through a filter of several modifying smaller scale processes before their impact on plot scale community structure is manifested.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sejr, Mikael Kristian","Mouritsen, Kim Nørgaard","Krause-Jensen, Dorte","Olesen, Birgit","Blicher, Martin Emil","Thyrring, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-141728"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Greenland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","University of California at Berkeley"],"keyword":["Algae","Arctic","Community structure","Greenland","Intertidal","Sea ice"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"small scale factors modify impacts of temperature ice scour and waves and drive rocky intertidal community structure in a greenland fjord","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmars.2020.607135","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-141728","identifier":[{"id":"85100579745","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1562e720-15d5-4882-a46f-044109e78ccc"],"keyword":["Arctic","Greenland","algae","community structure","intertidal","sea ice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51250DD1237519053970185A73D269B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmars.2020.607135","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/264401574/fmars_07_607135.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Center, ECOS Water","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael Kristian","key":"sejrpau","last":"Sejr","locid":"6c688ffc-6794-4482-b9b9-131b3dbf4206","name":"Sejr, Mikael Kristian","orcid":"0000-0001-8370-5791","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Nørgaard","key":"mouritsenpau","last":"Mouritsen","locid":"8b86816b-2691-4a1c-9bf8-bd1bd7a646fd","name":"Mouritsen, Kim Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3564-8328","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte","key":"krausejensenpau","last":"Krause-Jensen","locid":"f866cf43-1206-44ac-98aa-dd2f160cc85c","name":"Krause-Jensen, Dorte","orcid":"0000-0001-9792-256X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"adb70a49-eced-4c10-ac96-9fcffe90e6b3","name":"Olesen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-8864-6716","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Emil","key":"blicherpau","last":"Blicher","name":"Blicher, Martin Emil","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"thyrringpau","last":"Thyrring","locid":"85aae02b-373b-47d4-9fdb-5afb22b7d85c","name":"Thyrring, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-1029-3105","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmars.2020.607135","issn":["22967745"],"journal":"Frontiers in Marine Science","paperid":"607135","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Marine Science","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100579745"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1562e720-15d5-4882-a46f-044109e78ccc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Small Scale Factors Modify Impacts of Temperature, Ice Scour and Waves and Drive Rocky Intertidal Community Structure in a Greenland Fjord","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-141728","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Climate change has ecosystem-wide cascading effects. Little is known, however, about the resilience of Arctic marine ecosystems to environmental change. Here we quantify and compare large-scale patterns in rocky intertidal biomass, coverage and zonation in six regions along a north-south gradient of temperature and ice conditions in West Greenland (60–72°N). We related the level and variation in assemblage composition, biomass and coverage to latitudinal-scale environmental drivers. Across all latitudes, the intertidal assemblage was dominated by a core of stress-tolerant foundation species that constituted > 95% of the biomass. Hence, canopy-forming macroalgae, represented by Fucus distichus subsp. evanescens and F. vesiculosus and, up to 69°N, also Ascophyllum nodosum, together with Semibalanus balanoides, occupied > 70% of the vertical tidal range in all regions. Thus, a similar functional assemblage composition occurred across regions, and no latitudinal depression was observed. The most conspicuous difference in species composition from south to north was that three common species (the macroalgae Ascophyllum nodosum, the amphipod Gammarus setosus and the gastropod Littorina obtusata) disappeared from the mid-intertidal, although at different latitudes. There were no significant relationships between assemblage metrics and air temperature or sea ice coverage as obtained from weather stations and satellites, respectively. Although the mean biomass decreased > 50% from south to north, local biomass in excess of 10 000 g ww m −2 was found even at the northernmost site, demonstrating the patchiness of this habitat and the effect of small-scale variation in environmental characteristics. Hence, using the latitudinal gradient in a space-for-time substitution, our results suggest that while climate modification may lead to an overall increase in the intertidal biomass in north Greenland, it is unlikely to drive dramatic functional changes in ecosystem structure in the near future. Our dataset provides an important baseline for future studies to verify these predictions for Greenland's intertidal zone.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Thyrring, Jakob","Wegeberg, Susse","Blicher, Martin E.","Krause-Jensen, Dorte","Høgslund, Signe","Olesen, Birgit","Jozef, Wiktor","Mouritsen, Kim Nørgaard","Peck, Lloyd S.","Sejr, Mikael Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-207623"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thyrring, Jakob"],"country":["Greenland","Poland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","British Antarctic Survey","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Polish Academy of Sciences","University of California at Berkeley"],"keyword":["Arctic","Arctic fjord","Benthos","Biogeography","Blue mussels","Climate change","Community composition","Freezing tolerance","Mytilus edulis","Performance","Range shifts","SHIFTS","Temperature","ZONE","sea ice cover"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"latitudinal patterns in intertidal ecosystem structure in west greenland suggest resilience to climate change","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ecog.05381","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-207623","identifier":[{"id":"000648084500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85105216250","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-893c6d57-8ea5-4324-afbf-2a72d4931efc"],"keyword":["ARCTIC FJORD","Arctic","BLUE MUSSELS","COMMUNITY COMPOSITION","FREEZING TOLERANCE","MYTILUS-EDULIS","PERFORMANCE","SEA-ICE COVER","SHIFTS","TEMPERATURE","ZONE","benthos","biogeography","climate change","range shifts","space-for-time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-19B82E6AE4692B70EC35235FA312F763"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/264401620/ecog.05381_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ecog.05381","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"british antarctic survey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"British Antarctic Survey","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Centre, Roskilde","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"pl","key":"polish academy of sciences","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polish Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"thyrringpau","last":"Thyrring","name":"Thyrring, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Susse","key":"wegebergpau","last":"Wegeberg","locid":"05370847-e1d3-4253-b818-046251260ff5","name":"Wegeberg, Susse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin E.","key":"blicherpau","last":"Blicher","name":"Blicher, Martin E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte","key":"krausejensenpau","last":"Krause-Jensen","locid":"f866cf43-1206-44ac-98aa-dd2f160cc85c","name":"Krause-Jensen, Dorte","orcid":"0000-0001-9792-256X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe","key":"hogslundpau","last":"Hogslund","locid":"a16b561b-3a9e-45a8-b2df-b298312e4ab1","name":"Høgslund, Signe","name_org":"Hogslund, Signe","orcid":"0000-0001-5926-8464","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"adb70a49-eced-4c10-ac96-9fcffe90e6b3","name":"Olesen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-8864-6716","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Wiktor","key":"jozefpau","last":"Jozef","name":"Jozef, Wiktor","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim N.","key":"mouritsenpau","last":"Mouritsen","locid":"8b86816b-2691-4a1c-9bf8-bd1bd7a646fd","name":"Mouritsen, Kim Nørgaard","name_org":"Mouritsen, Kim N.","orcid":"0000-0003-3564-8328","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lloyd S.","key":"peckpau","last":"Peck","name":"Peck, Lloyd S.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael K.","key":"sejrpau","last":"Sejr","locid":"6c688ffc-6794-4482-b9b9-131b3dbf4206","name":"Sejr, Mikael Kristian","name_org":"Sejr, Mikael K.","orcid":"0000-0001-8370-5791","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ecog.05381","issn":["09067590","16000587"],"issn_org":["09067590"],"issue":"8","journal":"Ecography","pages":"1156-1168","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Ecography","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105216250"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-893c6d57-8ea5-4324-afbf-2a72d4931efc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Latitudinal patterns in intertidal ecosystem structure in West Greenland suggest resilience to climate change","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-207623","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"De-identification is the task of detecting privacy-related entities in text, such as person names, emails and contact data. It has been well-studied within the medical domain. The need for de-identification technology is increasing, as privacy-preserving data handling is in high demand in many domains. In this paper, we focus on job postings. We present JobStack, a new corpus for de-identification of personal data in job vacancies on Stackoverflow. We introduce baselines, comparing Long-Short Term Memory (LSTM) and Transformer models. To improve upon these baselines, we experiment with contextualized embeddings and distantly related auxiliary data via multi-task learning. Our results show that auxiliary data improves de-identification performance.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","Zhang, Mike","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382435"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Baselines","De identification","Job postings","JobStack corpus","Long short term memory LSTM","Medical domain","Personal data","Privacy preserving data","Privacy related entities","Transformer models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de identification of privacy related entities in job postings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85880206/JobStack_NoDaLiDa_2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382435","ids":["itu-4e400a88-6fcb-4ba1-ae10-675b004fd96f"],"keyword":["Baselines","De-identification","Job postings","JobStack corpus","Long-Short Term Memory (LSTM)","Medical domain","Personal data","Privacy-preserving data","Privacy-related entities","Transformer models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A318D3CE2066B5BFD8857202C992945A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85880206/JobStack_NoDaLiDa_2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Nørgaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"04344edd-2f02-45d5-ad45-baffe4c08898","name":"Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"21","pages":"210-221","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","series":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 23rd Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4e400a88-6fcb-4ba1-ae10-675b004fd96f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"De-identification of Privacy-related Entities in Job Postings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382435","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The aim of this work was to evaluate the prognostic impact of statin therapy in symptomatic patients without obstructive CAD. Background: Information on the prognostic impact of post–coronary computed tomographic angiography (CTA) statin use in patients with no or nonobstructive coronary artery disease (CAD) is sparse. Methods: Patients undergoing CTA with suspected CAD in western Denmark from 2008 to 2017 with <50% coronary stenoses were identified. Information on post-CTA use of statin therapy and cardiovascular events were obtained from national registries. Results: The study included 33,552 patients, median aged 56 years, 58% female, with no (n = 19,669) or nonobstructive (n = 13,883) CAD and a median follow-up of 3.5 years. The absolute risk of the combined end point of myocardial infarction (MI) or all-cause mortality was directly associated with the CAD burden with an event rate/1,000 patient-years of 4.13 (95% CI: 3.69-4.61) in no, 7.74 (95% CI: 6.88-8.71) in mild (coronary artery calcium score [CACS] 0-99), 13.72 (95% CI: 11.61-16.23) in moderate (CACS 100-399), and 32.47 (95% CI: 26.25-40.16) in severe (CACS ≥400) nonobstructive CAD. Statin therapy was associated with a multivariable adjusted HR for MI and death of 0.52 (95% CI: 0.36-0.75) in no, 0.44 (95% CI: 0.32-0.62) in mild, 0.51 (95% CI: 0.34-0.75) in moderate, and 0.52 (95% CI: 0.32-0.86) in severe nonobstructive CAD. The estimated numbers needed to treat to prevent the primary end point were 92 (95% CI: 61-182) in no, 36 (95% CI: 26-58) in mild, 24 (95% CI: 15-61) in moderate, and 13 (95% CI: 7-86) in severe nonobstructive CAD. Residual confounding may persist, but not to an extent explaining all of the observed risk reduction associated with statin treatment. Conclusions: The risk of MI and all-cause mortality in patients without obstructive CAD is directly associated with the CAD burden. Statin therapy is associated with a reduction of MI and all-cause death across the spectrum of CAD, however, the absolute benefit of treatment is directionally proportional with the CAD burden.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Øvrehus, Kristian A","Diederichsen, Axel","Grove, Erik Lerkevang","Steffensen, Flemming H","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Mickley, Hans","Nielsen, Lene H","Busk, Martin","Sand, Niels Peter R","Lambrechtsen, Jess","Riis, Anders H","Andersen, Ina Trolle","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S02-092.07-025441"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Øvrehus, Kristian Altern"],"keyword":["Coronary Angiography methods","Coronary artery disease","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl CoA Reductase Inhibitors therapeutic use","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction etiology","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Severity of Illness Index","Statins","coronary CTA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reduction of myocardial infarction and all cause mortality associated to statins in patients without obstructive cad","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85119511119","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.07-025441","identifier":[{"id":"34274285","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85119511119","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-af694a87-a05a-4131-a0d0-03b970bafea1","sdu-c42acee4-eb4d-46d8-a199-b218bd8ca76e"],"keyword":["Coronary Angiography/methods","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA Reductase Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction/etiology","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Severity of Illness Index","coronary CTA","coronary artery disease","statins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-66B641A9CDF801D214BC780F8FBE46F7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian A","key":"øvrehuspau","last":"Øvrehus","locid":"aec90a0e-8351-489e-8ab9-7b0829c8f1a6","name":"Øvrehus, Kristian Altern","name_org":"Øvrehus, Kristian A","orcid":"0000-0003-2454-5446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","locid":"d84be6bc-52bf-4710-9f66-0209cfab4f54","name":"Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Py