rnal of the American College of Cardiology","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096850312"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-393a0c9f-66e2-41c0-8f68-e435ac0a9960","au-82afdd2a-73a4-40dc-bded-64106d1a5a0d","sdu-7df54bec-44c7-4a4c-9a8a-b1bcc3176063"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of Plaque Burden Versus Stenosis on Ischemic Events in Patients With Coronary Atherosclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-002841","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces DAN+, a new multi-domain corpus and annotation guidelines for Dan- ish nested named entities (NEs) and lexical normalization to support research on cross-lingual cross-domain learning for a less-resourced language. We empirically assess three strategies to model the two-layer Named Entity Recognition (NER) task. We compare transfer capabilities from German versus in-language annotation from scratch. We examine language-specific versus multilingual BERT, and study the effect of lexical normalization on NER. Our results show that 1) the most robust strategy is multi-task learning which is rivaled by multi-label decoding, 2) BERT-based NER models are sensitive to domain shifts, and 3) in-language BERT and lexical normalization are the most beneficial on the least canonical data. Our results also show that an out-of-domain setup remains challenging, while performance on news plateaus quickly. This highlights the importance of cross-domain evaluation of cross-lingual transfer.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Plank, Barbara","Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383272"],"event":{"acronym":"COLING","title":"International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross lingual transfer","DAN Corpus","Lexical normalization","Nested Named Entities","multilingual BERT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dan danish nested named entities and lexical normalization","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85472827/COLING2020_Dan_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383272","ids":["itu-88b35a1e-6d89-4cba-808a-3982512880f6"],"keyword":["Cross-lingual Transfer","DAN+ Corpus","Lexical Normalization","Multilingual BERT","Nested Named Entities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AFF085C79F69B0DBDEBD247EFCAE0922"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85472827/COLING2020_Dan_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Nørgaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"04344edd-2f02-45d5-ad45-baffe4c08898","name":"Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"6649-6662","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"The 28th International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-88b35a1e-6d89-4cba-808a-3982512880f6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DAN+: Danish Nested Named Entities and Lexical Normalization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383272","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: This study aimed to assess if information on CAD severity from coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA) can identify patients that benefit most from treating low-density lipoprotein-cholesterol (LDL-C) to American Heart Association/American College of Cardiology (ACC/AHA) and European Society of Cardiology (ESC) guidelines targets. Background: Current treatment guidelines for secondary prevention of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) disregard severity of coronary artery disease (CAD) for treatment choices. It is unclear whether severity of CAD should be considered in treatment recommendations. Methods: Among 20,241 symptomatic patients undergoing diagnostic CTA from the Western Denmark Heart Registry, we assessed the number needed to treat (NNT) in 6 years to prevent 1 ASCVD event as well as the proportion of all events that could be prevented by treating LDL-C to targets. We assumed a 22% relative reduction of ASCVD events per 1 mmol/l reduction in LDL-C. Results: In multivariable analysis with no CAD as the reference, the subdistribution hazard ratio for ASCVD events was 4.0 (95% confidence interval [CI]: 3.3 to 4.9) for 1-vessel disease, 4.6 (3.5 to 6.0) for 2-vessel disease, and 5.6 (4.0 to 8.0) for 3-vessel disease. Consequently, the NNT to prevent 1 ASCVD event in 6 years by treating LDL-C to targets varied greatly from 233 (ESC) and 110 (ACC/AHA) for patients with no CAD to 8-9 for patients with 3-vessel disease (both ACC/AHA and ESC). The estimated percentage of ASCVD events that could be prevented by achieving guideline targets was 30% to 36% for patients with obstructive disease. However, <20% of patients achieved targets. Conclusions: An individualized approach based on CAD severity can identify symptomatic patients that are likely to derive most and least benefit from treating LDL-C to ACC/AHA and ESC treatment targets.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Steffensen, Flemming Hald","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Rønnow Sand, Niels Peter","Kragholm, Kristian","Kanstrup, Helle","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Leipsic, Jonathon","Blaha, Michael J.","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S03-099.42-005619"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mortensen, Martin Bødtker"],"country":["Canada","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Canada","Johns Hopkins Ciccarone Center for the Prevention of Heart Disease","Johns Hopkins Medical Institutions","Johns Hopkins University","St. Paul's Hospital","University of British Columbia"],"keyword":["Guidelines","Prevention","Statins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cad severity on cardiac cta identifies patients with most benefit of treating ldl cholesterol to acc aha and esc eas targets","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85089898623","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was funded by Aarhus University Hospital. The funding source had no role in design, conduct, analysis, or reporting of this study. Dr. Blaha has received grants from the National Institutes of Health, U.S. Food and Drug Administration, American Heart Association, and Aetna Foundation; grants and personal fees from Amgen; and personal fees from Sanofi, Regeneron, Novartis, Bayer, and Novo Nordisk outside the submitted work. All other authors have reported that they have no relationships relevant to the contents of this paper to disclose."],"id":"S03-099.42-005619","identifier":[{"id":"85089898623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32563656","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-73f1ca22-f63a-4ecf-9591-486b490e0f5f","au-87669013-fd66-4c64-a034-73d63e0ecb0d","sdu-83133d35-4cf8-4fad-a073-0a21dc7886cf"],"keyword":["guidelines","prevention","statins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-215065BE0F6CF57D1DCE72BA592F4831"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Cardiology (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, 