-039a9338cd4c","name":"Rohold, Allan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29909103"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcmg.2018.05.004","issn":["18767591","1936878X"],"issn_org":["1936878X"],"issue":"11","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"1640-1650","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Imaging","title_org":"J A C C: Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048595771"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-97174406-6086-4132-ab4e-e661732ab5a4","au-5175ce19-b753-4c96-9cae-910bf2a7591c","sdu-6666ef05-2f6e-48e3-bc14-2888e012b350"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prospective Comparison of FFR Derived From Coronary CT Angiography With SPECT Perfusion Imaging in Stable Coronary Artery Disease : The ReASSESS Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.42-007323","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Coronary stenosis and plaque evaluation by coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA) may contribute to identify hemodynamically relevant lesions. We evaluated the most stenotic lesion including plaques proximal to it versus a total vessel analyses combined with stenosis for ischemia. METHODS: Patients scheduled for clinically indicated invasive coronary angiography (ICA) for suspected coronary artery disease underwent coronary CTA and ICA including fractional flow reserve (FFR) as part of the NXT trial (clinicaltrials.govNCT01757678). Stenoses were visually graded ≤50%, 51-70%, and >70% on coronary CTA. Semi-automated plaque analyses were performed using a proximal to the FFR pressure sensor location (including the most severe lesion to the coronary ostium) versus a total vessel (vessel diameter ≥2 mm) approach. Coronary stenosis and plaque parameters were evaluated for discrimination of ischemia by logistic regressions and combined models analyzed using receiver operating characteristics (ROC) with invasive FFR≤ 0.80 as reference standard. RESULTS: In 254 patients, mean (±SD) age 64 (±10) years, 64% male, a coronary CTA stenosis >50% was present in 239 (49%) vessels. Invasive FFR was ≤0.80 in 100 (21%) vessels. Coronary stenosis severity and low-density non-calcified plaque (LD-NCP) volume were independent predictors of ischemia in the \"proximal\" and \"total-vessel\" analyses. Stenosis severity + total vessel LD-NCP assessment performed better than stenosis severity + proximal LD-NCP evaluation (Area under curve [AUC] (95%CI): 0.83 (0.78-0.87) vs 0.81 (0.76-0.86), p-value = 0.009), whereas stenosis severity + proximal LD-NCP performed better than stenosis alone (AUC (95%CI): 0.81 (0.76-0.86) vs 0.78 (0.73-0.83), p-value = 0.019). CONCLUSION: Adding total vessel high-risk plaque volume to stenosis severity improves discrimination of ischemia in coronary CTA performed in patients with stable angina pectoris.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Øvrehus, Kristian A","Gaur, Sara","Leipsic, Jonathon","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Dey, Damini","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Ahmadi, Amir","Achenbach, Stephan","Ko, Brian","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S02-099.85-014858"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Øvrehus, Kristian Altern"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cedars-Sinai Comprehensive Cancer Center","Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Monash University","St. Pauls Hospital","University of Erlangen-Nuremberg, Germany"],"keyword":["Aged","Angina Stable diagnostic imaging","Area Under Curve","Cardiac Catheterization","Chi Square Distribution","Computed Tomography Angiography","Coronary Angiography methods","Coronary Artery Disease diagnostic imaging","Coronary Stenosis diagnostic imaging","Coronary Vessels diagnostic imaging","Female","Fractional Flow Reserve Myocardial","Hemodynamics","Humans","Linear Models","Logistic Models","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Plaque Atherosclerotic","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","ROC Curve","Reproducibility of Results","Severity of Illness Index"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ct based total vessel plaque analyses improves prediction of hemodynamic significance lesions as assessed by fractional flow reserve in patients with stable angina pectoris","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85047818499","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.85-014858","identifier":[{"id":"29866619","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85047818499","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1f078fe3-6d0a-4eec-8a4f-17bd86e4b989","sdu-a1e6d5b2-ef0c-4183-b2ca-6aeeb4d1104d"],"keyword":["Aged","Angina, Stable/diagnostic imaging","Area Under Curve","Cardiac Catheterization","Chi-Square Distribution","Computed Tomography Angiography","Coronary Angiography/methods","Coronary Artery Disease/diagnostic imaging","Coronary Stenosis/diagnostic imaging","Coronary Vessels/diagnostic imaging","Female","Fractional Flow Reserve, Myocardial","Hemodynamics","Humans","Linear Models","Logistic Models","Male","Middle Aged","Multidetector Computed Tomography","Plaque, Atherosclerotic","Predictive Value of Tests","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","ROC Curve","Reproducibility of Results","Severity of Illness Index"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0C1F03075DEBFD6976CF5143EAEEE2F0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"st pauls hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"St. Pauls Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"cedars sinai medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"cedars sinai comprehensive cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cedars-Sinai Comprehensive Cancer Center","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"icahn school of medicine at mount sinai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"de","key":"friedrich alexander university erlangen nürnberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"de","key":"university of erlangen nuremberg germany","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Erlangen-Nuremberg, Germany","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian A.","key":"øvrehuspau","last":"Øvrehus","locid":"aec90a0e-8351-489e-8ab9-7b0829c8f1a6","name":"Øvrehus, Kristian Altern","name_org":"Øvrehus, Kristian A.","orcid":"0000-0003-2454-5446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"gaurpau","last":"Gaur","locid":"6330bb47-6e95-4cd6-8c84-70769abd0122","name":"Gaur, Sara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathon","key":"leipsicpau","last":"Leipsic","name":"Leipsic, Jonathon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper M","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","name_org":"Jensen, Jesper M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Damini","key":"deypau","last":"Dey","name":"Dey, Damini","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans E","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","name_org":"Bøtker, Hans E","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Amir","key":"ahmadipau","last":"Ahmadi","name":"Ahmadi, Amir","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"achenbachpau","last":"Achenbach","name":"Achenbach, Stephan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian","key":"kopau","last":"Ko","name":"Ko, Brian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne L","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","name_org":"Nørgaard, Bjarne L","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29866619"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcct.2018.04.008","issn":["1876861X","19345925"],"issn_org":["19345925"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Computed Tomography","pages":"344-349","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Computed Tomography","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047818499"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1f078fe3-6d0a-4eec-8a4f-17bd86e4b989","sdu-a1e6d5b2-ef0c-4183-b2ca-6aeeb4d1104d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"CT-based total vessel plaque analyses improves prediction of hemodynamic significance lesions as assessed by fractional flow reserve in patients with stable angina pectoris","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.85-014858","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objectives We aimed to investigate if lesion-specific ischaemia by invasive fractional flow reserve (FFR) can be predicted by an integrated machine learning (ML) ischaemia risk score from quantitative plaque measures from coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA). Methods In a multicentre trial of 254 patients, CTA and invasive coronary angiography were performed, with FFR in 484 vessels. CTA data sets were analysed by semi-automated software to quantify stenosis and non-calcified (NCP), low-density NCP (LD-NCP, < 30 HU), calcified and total plaque volumes, contrast density difference (CDD, maximum difference in luminal attenuation per unit area) and plaque length. ML integration included automated feature selection and model building from quantitative CTA with a boosted ensemble algorithm, and tenfold stratified cross-validation. Results Eighty patients had ischaemia by FFR (FFR ≤ 0.80) in 100 vessels. Information gain for predicting ischaemia was highest for CDD (0.172), followed by LD-NCP (0.125), NCP (0.097), and total plaque volumes (0.092). ML exhibited higher area-under-the-curve (0.84) than individual CTA measures, including stenosis (0.76), LD-NCP volume (0.77), total plaque volume (0.74) and pre-test likelihood of coronary artery disease (CAD) (0.63); p < 0.006. Conclusions Integrated ML ischaemia risk score improved the prediction of lesion-specific ischaemia by invasive FFR, over stenosis, plaque measures and pre-test likelihood of CAD.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Dey, Damini","Gaur, Sara","Øvrehus, Kristian A","Slomka, Piotr J","Betancur, Julian","Goeller, Markus","Hell, Michaela M","Gransar, Heidi","Berman, Daniel S","Achenbach, Stephan","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-231465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrated prediction of lesion specific ischaemia from quantitative coronary ct angiography using machine learning a multicentre study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5940537/pdf/nihms936161.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-231465","identifier":[{"id":"29352380","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5940537","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85040640232","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b2fe8fee-eb9c-4926-8fa2-e4c03a3a8345"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46525DDBB432A189DB3AAEFBD370ED6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5940537/pdf/nihms936161.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"cedars sinai medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"friedrich alexander university erlangen nürnberg","loc":["Ger