,"name":"Maeng, Michael","name_org":"Mæng, Michael","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen D","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"6d64271d-8a2c-41ea-891d-e85555bbd47a","name":"Kristensen, Steen Dalby","name_org":"Kristensen, Steen D","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars R","key":"krusellpau","last":"Krusell","locid":"660b49df-f279-4bc2-8ff9-50fe259b2d33","name":"Krusell, Lars Romer","name_org":"Krusell, Lars R","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens F","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"569ae3f1-67b8-4b02-9b3f-6469767f33e3","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","name_org":"Lassen, Jens F","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper M","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","name_org":"Jensen, Jesper M","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28862968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.117.005587","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e005587","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030699040"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-24d7d104-41e4-48c9-86cf-d0ed73adf683","sdu-c266f0c7-34cb-4a33-b696-043ee021e2d7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Myocardial Perfusion Imaging Versus Computed Tomography Angiography-Derived Fractional Flow Reserve Testing in Stable Patients With Intermediate-Range Coronary Lesions : Influence on Downstream Diagnostic Workflows and Invasive Angiography Findings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-015277","year":"2017","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Background We hypothesize that in patients with suspected coronary artery disease (CAD), lower values of the ratio of total epicardial coronary arterial lumen volume to left ventricular myocardial mass (V/M) result in lower fractional flow reserve (FFR). Methods V/M was computed in 238 patients from the NXT trial who underwent coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), quantitative coronary angiography (QCA) and FFR measurement in 438 vessels. Nitroglycerin was administered prior to CT, QCA and FFR acquisition. The V/M ratio was quantified on a patient-level from CT image data by segmenting the epicardial coronary arterial lumen volume (V) and the left ventricular myocardial mass (M). Calcified and noncalcified plaque volumes were quantified using semi-automated software. Results The median value of V/M (18.57 mm 3/g) was used to define equal groups of low and high V/M patients. Patients with low V/M had greater diameter stenosis by QCA, more plaque and lower FFR (0.80 ± 0.12 vs. 0.87 ± 0.08; P < 0.0001) than those with high V/M. A total of 365 vessels in 202 patients had QCA stenosis ≤50% and measured FFR. In these patients, those with low V/M had higher percent diameter stenosis by QCA, greater total plaque volume and lower FFR (0.81 ± 0.12 vs. 0.88 ± 0.07; P < 0.0001) than those with high V/M. In multivariate logistic regression analysis, V/M was an independent predictor of FFR ≤0.80 (all p-values < 0.001). Conclusions Patients with a low V/M ratio have lower FFR overall and in non-obstructive CAD, independent of plaque measures.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Taylor, Charles A","Gaur, Sara","Leipsic, Jonathon","Achenbach, Stephan","Berman, Daniel S","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Dey, Damini","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Kim, Hyun Jin","Khem, Sophie","Wilk, Alan","Zarins, Christopher K","Bezerra, Hiram","Lesser, John","Ko, Brian","Narula, Jagat","Ahmadi, Amir","Øvrehus, Kristian A","St Goar, Fred","De Bruyne, Bernard","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-208576"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Canada","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cardiovascular Center Aalst","Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","El Camino Hospital Mountain View","Heartflow Inc.","Monash University","Mount Sinai Health","St. Pauls Hospital","Stanford University","University Hospitals of Cleveland","Universitätsklinikum Erlangen"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of the ratio of coronary arterial lumen volume to left ventricle myocardial mass derived from coronary ct angiography on fractional flow reserve","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85026777884","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-208576","identifier":[{"id":"28789941","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85026777884","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8ae000be-7fcc-4015-a630-c242ef07ac2c"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A41A1D925DF00AD4638C96637B362EAD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"st pauls hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"St. Pauls Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"universitätsklinikum erlangen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universitätsklinikum Erlangen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"cedars sinai medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"heartflow inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Heartflow Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"university hospitals of cleveland","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University Hospitals of Cleveland","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"mount sinai health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Mount Sinai Health","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"us","key":"el camino hospital mountain view","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"El Camino Hospital Mountain View","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"be","key":"cardiovascular center aalst","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Cardiovascular Center Aalst","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles A","key":"taylorpau","last":"Taylor","name":"Taylor, Charles A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"gaurpau","last":"Gaur","locid":"63