","last":"Møller","locid":"5db09d5d-dbed-4d96-a000-a1681016491c","name":"Møller, Arne","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aage Kristian Olsen","key":"alstruppau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"fa66f5b8-0468-4e85-b570-969776c5ebde","name":"Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","orcid":"0000-0002-0084-9122","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leif","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"af45ec8c-f95a-4937-9e48-ffabe2b8933d","name":"Østergaard, Leif","orcid":"0000-0003-2930-6997","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Reidies","key":"bjarkampau","last":"Bjarkam","locid":"a1770adc-a79f-434a-98bc-02e64ffd13cd","name":"Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21867797"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/b978-0-444-53815-4.00014-5","issn":["00796123","18757855"],"issn_org":["00796123"],"journal":"Progress in Brain Research","pages":"97-103","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Progress in Brain Research","volume":"194"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80051887844"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e4f7b18d-8e9a-40d3-8753-063785ae611f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Development of neuromodulation treatments in a large animal model : Do neurosurgeons dream of electric pigs?","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-260067","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"It has been proposed that the increasing use of coronary computed tomographic angiography (CTA) may introduce additional unnecessary diagnostic procedures. However, no previous study has assessed the impact on downstream test utilization of conventional diagnostic testing relative to CTA in patients suspected of angina. The purpose of this study was to investigate the consequences of frontline exercise-stress testing (Ex-test) versus CTA on downstream test utilization in clinical practice. In two collaborating departments using either Ex-test (n = 247) or CTA (n = 251) as the frontline diagnostic test in patients suspected of angina, comparable cohorts of consecutive patients were retrospectively identified (Jan. 2007-Feb. 2008). Downstream test utilization (invasive coronary angiography, ICA; myocardial perfusion scintigraphy, and CTA) during 12 months after the index diagnostic test was recorded. Mean age was 56 years (51% men), and 96% of the total study cohort were at low-intermediate pretest risk of significant coronary disease. Overall, downstream test utilization was more frequent in the Ex-test group than in the CTA group, 32% versus 21% (P = 0.003). Subsequent myocardial scintigraphy was more frequent used (9% versus 4%, P = 0.03), whereas ICA tended to be more frequent applied in the Ex-test versus CTA group (23% vs. 18%, P = 0.15). A frontline diagnostic use in symptomatic patients of Ex-test in comparison to CTA leads to more downstream diagnostic test utilization. Future prospective trials are needed in order to define the most cost-effective diagnostic use of CTA relative to conventional ischemia testing.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, L. H.","Markenvard, John","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Mickley, Hans","Øvrehus, Kristian A","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde"],"cuid":["S02-097.87-013384"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Angina pectoris","Chi Square Distribution","Coronary Angiography","Coronary artery disease","Denmark","Exercise Test","Female","Health Resources","Humans","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Ischemia","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Predictive Value of Tests","Retrospective Studies","Time Factors","Tomography X Ray Computed"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"frontline diagnostic evaluation of patients suspected of angina by coronary computed tomography reduces downstream resource utilization when compared to conventional ischemia testing","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10554-010-9737-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.87-013384","identifier":[{"id":"21042860","type":"pmid"},{"id":"81255143571","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0ace3724-1196-4d0f-aa5e-a658973665c5","sdu-77d11aa4-cffc-4e99-809d-9de616e0cbe0"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Angina Pectoris","Chi-Square Distribution","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease","Denmark","Exercise Test","Female","Health Resources","Humans","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Ischemia","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Predictive Value of Tests","Retrospective Studies","Time Factors","Tomography, X-Ray Computed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3CD4C7ACE6267BB6A9169C21288042FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10554-010-9737-6","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afd., Fredericia"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"L. H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, L. H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"markenvardpau","last":"Markenvard","locid":"1464f2af-2504-4a8d-8b53-438b4f36f5d4","name":"Markenvard, John","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"mickleypau","last":"Mickley","locid":"f6789f9a-e23b-4ab8-bd7d-a3c168107cdb","name":"Mickley, Hans","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Altern","key":"øvrehuspau","last":"Øvrehus","locid":"3a9366a8-3e88-4426-95a9-c26f820f6650","name":"Øvrehus, Kristian A","name_org":"Øvrehus, Kristian Altern","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian A","key":"ovrehuspau","last":"Ovrehus","name":"Ovrehus, Kristian A","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne Linde","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21042860"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10554-010-9737-6","issn":["15695794","18758312"],"issn_org":["15695794"],"issue":"6","journal":"The International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"813-23","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"The International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","title_org":"International Journal of Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-81255143571"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0ace3724-1196-4d0f-aa5e-a658973665c5","sdu-77d11aa4-cffc-4e99-809d-9de616e0cbe0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Frontline diagnostic evaluation of patients suspected of angina by coronary computed tomography reduces downstream resource utilization when compared to conventional ischemia testing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.87-013384","year":"2011","yearsub":2011}
{"abstract":"We evaluated the influence of coronary computed tomographic angiography (CTA) as a first-line diagnostic test on patient treatment and prognosis. A total of 1,055 consecutive patients with suspected stable angina pectoris (mean age 55 ± 10 years, 56% women) and a low to intermediate pretest likelihood of coronary artery disease (CAD) were included in the present study. The patients were followed for a median of 18 months. The use of downstream diagnostic testing and medical therapy after CTA were recorded. The CTA result was normal in 49%, and nonobstructive and obstructive CAD (≥50% stenosis) was demonstrated in 31% and 15% of the patients, respectively. Coronary CTA was inconclusive in 5% of the patients. The use of antiplatelet therapy decreased with normal findings from CTA, and the use of antiplatelet and lipid-lowering agents increased in patients with CAD. Additional testing was performed in 2% of patients with normal CTA findings and in 7% and 82% of patients with nonobstructive or obstructive CAD, respectively. No patients without CAD, 0.9% of patients with nonobstructive CAD, and 1.9% of patients with obstructive CAD met the primary end point (cardiovascular death and myocardial infarction, p = 0.008). No patients without CAD, 1.5% of patients with nonobstructive CAD, and 30% patients with obstructive CAD met the secondary end point (cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction, and coronary revascularization, p","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ovrehus, Kristian A","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Jensen, Jesper M","Munkholm, Henrik","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Nørgaard, Bjarne L"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244846"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Angina pectoris","Coronary Angiography","Coronary artery disease","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Hypolipidemic Agents","Male","Middle Aged","Platelet Aggregation Inhibitors","Prognosis","Tomography X Ray Computed"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of coronary computed tomographic angiography on patient treatment and prognosis in patients with suspected stable angina pectoris","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjcard.2011.01.024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244846","identifier":[{"id":"79955607688","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21420047","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ca3196fc-a254-49b9-9631-35987d2e4416"],"keyword":["Angina Pectoris","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Hypolipidemic Agents","Male","Middle Aged","Platelet Aggregation Inhibitors","Prognosis","Tomography, X-Ray Computed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DD7DBD859663E53BFB320191D48D9C92"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjcard.2011.01.024","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian A","key":"ovrehuspau","last":"Ovrehus","name":"Ovrehus, Kristian A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans E","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","name_org":"Bøtker, Hans E","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","correspondin